kdriver: gate fops_read/fops_write timeout logs behind #ifdef DEBUG

Re-applied at build time to the pinned mx3_driver_pub tag (v2.1.0). memx_fops_read
/memx_fops_write log an un-guarded info-level "wait timeout N(s), retrying again"
on every wait_event_interruptible_timeout() timeout and re-arm. On a healthy but
idle device (Frigate holding the accelerator between motion-gated detections) the
10s read timeout fires every ~10s indefinitely, flooding the kernel log. Every
other diagnostic in this file is already wrapped in #ifdef DEBUG; these two were
the only un-guarded ones. Our sysext builds non-DEBUG (kbuild EXTRA_CFLAGS has no
-DDEBUG), so wrapping them silences the spam while keeping them in debug builds.

No functional change (the wait loops are driven by while (wq_status < 1); the
gated if/pr_info was diagnostic only) and NO driver version change. Upstreamed as
scyto/mx3_driver_pub branch gate-fops-timeout-debug-logs (PR pending) -> the
applier skips this once it lands in the pinned tag.

diff --git a/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_cascade_pciemain.c b/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_cascade_pciemain.c
index 79cfa39..0eb9167 100644
--- a/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_cascade_pciemain.c
+++ b/kdriver/linux/pcie/memx_cascade_pciemain.c
@@ -470,8 +470,10 @@ static ssize_t memx_fops_read(struct file *filp, char __user *buf, size_t count,
 				break;
 			}
 
+#ifdef DEBUG
 			if (wq_status < 1)
 				pr_info("memryx: fops_read: wait timeout 10(s), retrying again\n");
+#endif
 
 		} while (wq_status < 1);
 		if (wq_status >= 1) {
@@ -564,8 +566,10 @@ static ssize_t memx_fops_write(struct file *filp, const char __user *buf, size_t
 			pr_warn("memryx: fops_write: cancelled by interrupt signal\n");
 			break;
 		}
+#ifdef DEBUG
 		if (wq_status < 1)
 			pr_info("memryx: fops_write: wait timeout 1(s), retrying again\n");
+#endif
 
 	} while (wq_status < 1);
 	if (wq_status >= 1) {
